# full_scan_template.mac — one ANGLE per macro, filled in by python/run_scan.py.
#
# Pass 5 will substitute {{PHANTOM}}, {{OUTPUT_FILE}}, {{ANGLE}} and
# {{TRANSLATION_BLOCK}}. The shape below is a consequence of two Pass 4
# decisions and is worth understanding before changing it.
#
# ONE PROCESS PER ANGLE, NOT PER MEASUREMENT (ADR 0005 / D2).
#   /cttwin/scan/... moves existing volumes and is legal after /run/initialize,
#   so the whole inner translation sweep runs inside one process. A 180 x 128
#   scan is ~180 launches instead of ~23,000. /cttwin/phantom stays above
#   /run/initialize because it rebuilds solids and is rejected afterwards.
#
# ONE FILE PER ANGLE.
#   /cttwin/output/file is set once; each /run/beamOn appends a row and the
#   header is written only for a new or empty file. 180 files, not 23,040 —
#   which retires the file-count warning in [[Output Format]] without moving
#   to HDF5.
#
# SEEDS ARE NOT OPTIONAL.
#   Every cttwin process starts from the same default seed, and runs within a
#   process draw sequentially from one stream. Without an explicit reseed per
#   measurement, the same noise realisation repeats at the same position in
#   every angle's sweep — correlated noise down a column of the sinogram, which
#   reconstructs into structured artefacts rather than grain. Pass 4 saw this
#   directly: inserting one extra /run/beamOn into a checkpoint macro shifted
#   every later run's counts by one position in a fixed sequence.
#
# {{TRANSLATION_BLOCK}} expands to one of these per translation step:
#
#     /random/setSeeds <s1> <s2>
#     /cttwin/output/projectionId <id>
#     /cttwin/scan/translation <t> mm
#     /run/beamOn <n_photons>
#
# THE OPEN BEAM.
#   Line integrals are -ln(N/N0), so N0 must be measured too. Under ADR 0005
#   the source and detector never move, so with /cttwin/phantom none there is
#   nothing in the world that changes with theta or t — every open-beam
#   measurement is the SAME simulation. One high-statistics open-beam run
#   suffices for the entire scan; a full open-beam sweep would just be that one
#   number resampled. Do not skip it, and do not scan it.

# THREADS ARE PINNED, AND PARALLELISM IS OVER ANGLES.
#   Pass 5 (D4). Angles are independent processes, so a pool of single-threaded
#   workers beats one MT process per angle: no per-run thread merge, no
#   start-up cost, and linear scaling. It also removes a variable nobody here
#   has measured — whether Geant4 11.2's event seeding is thread-count
#   independent depends on seedOncePerCommunication, and if it is not, then the
#   Pass 1-4 regression anchors are only reproducible at a fixed thread count.
#   Fixing the count sidesteps the question entirely.
#   /run/numberOfThreads is PRE-INIT ONLY, hence its position here.
#   `run_scan.py --anchors` verifies the anchors still hold at this setting.
/run/numberOfThreads 1

/run/verbose      0
/event/verbose    0
/tracking/verbose 0

/cttwin/phantom {{PHANTOM}}
/run/initialize

/cttwin/output/file {{OUTPUT_FILE}}
/cttwin/scan/angle {{ANGLE}} deg

{{TRANSLATION_BLOCK}}
